 never logged, and scrubbed from\nevery recorded error.",[198,210,211,214],{},[202,212,213],{},"Send test notification"," on the rule form sends a TEST to every enabled row and shows what each\none answered.",[216,217,219],"h2",{"id":218},"types","Types",[221,222,223,239],"table",{},[224,225,226],"thead",{},[227,228,229,233,236],"tr",{},[230,231,232],"th",{},"Type",[230,234,235],{},"Sends",[230,237,238],{},"Settings",[240,241,242,254,275,286,297,307,321,332,343,354],"tbody",{},[227,243,244,248,251],{},[245,246,247],"td",{},"Email",[245,249,250],{},"one email per recipient, with signed Acknowledge \u002F Resolve links",[245,252,253],{},"Recipients",[227,255,256,259,272],{},[245,257,258],{},"Webhook",[245,260,261,262,266,267,271],{},"generic JSON ",[263,264,265],"code",{},"{text, incident}"," (",[268,269,270],"a",{"href":169},"protocol",")",[245,273,274],{},"Webhook URL",[227,276,277,280,283],{},[245,278,279],{},"Raven",[245,281,282],{},"a message in a Raven channel",[245,284,285],{},"Raven Channel",[227,287,288,291,294],{},[245,289,290],{},"Slack",[245,292,293],{},"Block Kit message with a severity colour bar and Open \u002F Acknowledge \u002F Resolve buttons",[245,295,296],{},"Incoming Webhook URL*",[227,298,299,302,305],{},[245,300,301],{},"Mattermost",[245,303,304],{},"message attachment with colour, fields and Acknowledge \u002F Resolve links",[245,306,296],{},[227,308,309,312,318],{},[245,310,311],{},"Matrix",[245,313,314,317],{},[263,315,316],{},"m.room.message"," with an HTML body",[245,319,320],{},"Homeserver URL, Room ID, Access Token*",[227,322,323,326,329],{},[245,324,325],{},"ntfy",[245,327,328],{},"push with title, priority, tags, click and action buttons",[245,330,331],{},"Server URL (default ntfy.sh), Topic, Access Token* (optional)",[227,333,334,337,340],{},[245,335,336],{},"Gotify",[245,338,339],{},"push with priority mapped from severity and a click URL",[245,341,342],{},"Server URL, Application Token*",[227,344,345,348,351],{},[245,346,347],{},"SMS",[245,349,350],{},"short text (one or two SMS) through any HTTP gateway",[245,352,353],{},"Phone Numbers, Gateway URL template, Method, Body, Auth Header, Secret*, Max Length",[227,355,356,359,366],{},[245,357,358],{},"PagerDuty",[245,360,361,362,365],{},"Events API v2: trigger, acknowledge, resolve; ",[263,363,364],{},"dedup_key"," = incident name",[245,367,368],{},"Routing Key*, Events API URL",[198,370,371],{},"* Password field: stored encrypted, shown as asterisks.",[216,373,375],{"id":374},"who-hears-what","Who hears what",[377,378,379,389,403,409,412,431],"ul",{},[380,381,382,383,385,386,388],"li",{},"Opened and reopened incidents go to the ",[202,384,106],{},"; escalations to the ",[202,387,207],{},".",[380,390,391,392,394,395,398,399,402],{},"When someone acknowledges or resolves an incident (Desk or a signed link), ",[202,393,358],{}," channels\nalways get the matching ",[263,396,397],{},"acknowledge"," \u002F ",[263,400,401],{},"resolve"," event, so the alert closes on call too.",[380,404,405,406,388],{},"The other channels hear a resolution only when the rule has ",[202,407,408],{},"Notify On Resolve",[380,410,411],{},"A test from the rule form triggers then resolves on PagerDuty, so it never leaves an alert open.",[380,413,414,415,418,419,422,423,426,427,430],{},"With an ",[202,416,417],{},"hourly digest"," on a row, ",[263,420,421],{},"info"," and ",[263,424,425],{},"warning"," alerts are batched into one message per\ndestination. ",[263,428,429],{},"critical"," alerts are always immediate. PagerDuty is never digested.",[380,432,433,434,438],{},"During a ",[268,435,437],{"href":436},"\u002Falerts\u002Frules#maintenance-windows","maintenance window",", notifications wait until it ends.",[216,440,442],{"id":441},"signed-action-links","Signed action links",[198,444,445,446,398,449,452,453,456,457,460],{},"Alerts for unresolved incidents carry signed ",[202,447,448],{},"Acknowledge",[202,450,451],{},"Resolve"," links, valid 24 h\n(",[202,454,455],{},"Wolf Settings → Action Link Hours","). Opening a link shows a confirmation page; only its button\nacts, so mail scanners cannot acknowledge for you. Security incidents also carry a link per\n",[268,458,459],{"href":86},"response action"," Wolf proposes; those ask for a Wolf Manager's login.",[216,462,464],{"id":463},"delivery-status","Delivery status",[198,466,467,468,471,472,475],{},"Every attempt is recorded as a ",[202,469,470],{},"Wolf Delivery",": channel, target without secrets, kind, PagerDuty\naction, ok or error, HTTP status. The incident lists them under ",[202,473,474],{},"Deliveries",". Deliveries follow\nthe event retention.",[216,477,479],{"id":478},"setup-per-type","Setup per type",[481,482,483],"collapsible",{"name":290},[198,484,485,486,489,490,493,494,497],{},"Create an app → ",[202,487,488],{},"Incoming Webhooks"," → ",[202,491,492],{},"Add New Webhook to Workspace",", and paste the\n",[263,495,496],{},"https:\u002F\u002Fhooks.slack.com\u002Fservices\u002F…"," URL. Buttons open the incident or the signed action page, so no\nSlack interactivity endpoint is needed. Slack may show a warning icon on link buttons of apps\nwithout one.",[481,499,500],{"name":301},[198,501,502,505,506,509],{},[202,503,504],{},"Integrations → Incoming Webhooks → Add",", and paste the ",[263,507,508],{},"https:\u002F\u002F…\u002Fhooks\u002F…"," URL.",[481,511,512],{"name":311},[198,513,514,515,518,519,522,523,526,527,530,531,388],{},"Create a bot account, invite it to the room and join. Get its access token (Element: ",[202,516,517],{},"Settings →\nHelp & About → Access Token",", or ",[263,520,521],{},"POST \u002F_matrix\u002Fclient\u002Fv3\u002Flogin","). The Room ID is the internal\n",[263,524,525],{},"!…:server"," one (",[202,528,529],{},"Room settings → Advanced","), not an alias. Messages are sent with\n",[263,532,533],{},"PUT \u002F_matrix\u002Fclient\u002Fv3\u002Frooms\u002F{room}\u002Fsend\u002F…",[481,535,536],{"name":325},[198,537,538,539,542],{},"Any topic on ntfy.sh or your own server. On a public server, pick an unguessable topic, or protect it\nand paste an access token (",[263,540,541],{},"tk_…","). Priority: critical 5, warning 4, info 3, resolved 2; escalations\none step higher.",[481,544,545],{"name":336},[198,546,547,550],{},[202,548,549],{},"Apps → Create application",", and paste its token. Priority: critical 8, warning 5, info 3,\nresolved 2; escalations two steps higher.",[481,552,553,576,579],{"name":347},[198,554,555,556,559,560,563,564,567,568,571,572,575],{},"Provider agnostic. The Gateway URL and the optional Body Template take ",[263,557,558],{},"{to}",", ",[263,561,562],{},"{text}"," and\n",[263,565,566],{},"{secret}"," placeholders: URL-encoded in the URL and form bodies, JSON-escaped in JSON bodies. The Auth\nHeader is a header line such as ",[263,569,570],{},"Authorization: Bearer {secret}",". Put API keys in ",[202,573,574],{},"Secret",", never\nin the URL. One request per phone number.",[198,577,578],{},"The text (kind, severity, title, scope, and the incident URL when it fits) is folded to the GSM-7\nalphabet and cut on a word boundary to 160 characters (one SMS) or 306 (two). Text that needs\nUnicode fits 70 \u002F 134.",[580,581,588],"pre",{"className":582,"code":584,"filename":585,"language":586,"meta":587},[583],"language-text","Gateway URL:   https:\u002F\u002Fsms.example.com\u002Fapi\u002Fsend\nMethod \u002F Body: POST, json, {\"to\": \"{to}\", \"message\": \"{text}\"}\nAuth Header:   Authorization: Bearer {secret}\n","A gateway that takes JSON","text","",[263,589,584],{"__ignoreMap":587},[481,591,592],{"name":358},[198,593,594,595,598,599,602],{},"Add an ",[202,596,597],{},"Events API v2"," integration to a service and paste its integration key as the Routing Key.\nChange the Events API URL for the EU region (",[263,600,601],{},"https:\u002F\u002Fevents.eu.pagerduty.com\u002Fv2\u002Fenqueue","), or for an\nEvents-v2 compatible receiver: Grafana OnCall, Opsgenie and others accept the same body.",{"title":587,"searchDepth":604,"depth":605,"links":606},1,2,[607,608,609,610,611],{"id":218,"depth":605,"text":219},{"id":374,"depth":605,"text":375},{"id":441,"depth":605,"text":442},{"id":463,"depth":605,"text":464},{"id":478,"depth":605,"text":479},"Send alerts to email, chat, push, SMS or PagerDuty, and set up each destination.","md",null,{},{"icon":109},{"title":106,"description":612},"vgO3hEekSTPRUhYDRpY6BkCCnwZaG5IzftOER4fHlO0",[620,622],{"title":101,"path":102,"stem":103,"description":621,"icon":104},"The rules installed with the app, what each one watches, and when it fires.",{"title":111,"path":112,"stem":113,"description":623,"icon":114},"Acknowledge, assign, merge, split and close incidents, and write the postmortem.",1795011682747]